## Backend

Use Next.js server-side functionality and secure API routes or server actions where appropriate.

Keep business logic separated from UI components.

Use a service-oriented architecture so audio processing, document generation and AI services can be independently maintained.

## Database and authentication

Recommended platform: Supabase.

Use:
- Supabase PostgreSQL.
- Supabase Authentication.
- Supabase Storage.
- Row Level Security (RLS).
- Database migrations.
- Supabase Edge Functions when appropriate.

Authentication must support email and password initially, with Google sign-in as an optional integration.

## AI integration

Design an AI provider abstraction layer.

Support configurable integration with:
- OpenAI API.
- Other compatible AI providers in the future.

Use AI for:
- Summarization.
- Academic explanations.
- Question generation.
- Flashcard generation.
- Document analysis.
- Revision assistance.
- Study planning.

Do not hard-code one model throughout the application.

All model names, limits and provider settings must be configurable through environment variables or secure server-side configuration.

## Audio transcription

Design a separate transcription service.

Support integration with an appropriate speech-to-text provider.

Evaluate providers based on:
- English transcription accuracy.
- Support for Kenyan English accents.
- Swahili support where available.
- Long audio processing.
- Cost per audio minute.
- File-size restrictions.
- Processing time.
- Speaker diarization support.

